@design/delegation-service.sigil from DelegationService import {
  delegation, brief text, session cancel, completion notice, stop notice,
  status line, result text, queued task, collect tool,
}
@design/agent-config.sigil from AgentConfig import {
  tier word, tier text, unmatched tier text, agent alias, agent file,
  project root, SUBZERO_PROJECT_DIR, load error, general agent, model tier,
  medium tier, parallel limit, working directory,
}
@design/kernel.sigil from Kernel import {
  parent adapter, parent host, child host, entry point,
}
@design/task-core.sigil from TaskCore import {
  task id, attach command, child driver, transcript,
}
@design/task-store.sigil from TaskStore import { parent session id, task record }

component PiExtension {
  goal {
    Let a developer who works in the pi parent host run compound-engineering
    skills and have every subagent they start run as an isolated subzero child,
    on the model tier its request maps to in the agent file, or on the medium tier
    when it names none, with each task kept in the shared task record and
    a
    way to watch, collect and stop the children.
  }

  state {
    PiExtension is the parent adapter of the pi parent host. It runs inside the
    pi
    process as an extension that pi loads from a pi package. The entry point of
    that pi package is outside PiExtension: it creates a Kernel, registers a
    child driver for each child host it supports and registers PiExtension as the
    parent adapter pi.

    The *subagent tool* is the tool named subagent that PiExtension gives the
    pi
    parent host. Its request holds a brief text, an optional agent name, an
    optional
    model, which is the tier text, an optional async flag, optional files and
    an
    optional expected output.

    The *subzero tools* are the tools subzero_await, subzero_tasks and
    subzero_cancel. The tool subzero_await is the collect tool that the
    completion notice names, and it collects the result of tasks started without
    waiting,
    waits up to an *await timeout* that defaults to 30 seconds and never exceeds
    600
    seconds,
    and answers a task that has not settled with its status line. The tool
    subzero_tasks lists the tasks of the session core, and the tool
    subzero_cancel
    cancels one task by its task id or every task of the session core.

    A *session core* is the DelegationService that the entry point of the
    extension
    builds for one pi session, with the Kernel and the child drivers that only
    the
    entry point holds. Its parent session id is the session id of that pi
    session,
    and its project root is resolved from the working directory of that pi session.

    The *session widget* shows each Pending or live task of the session core
    with
    its model tier, its model and its elapsed time or its queue place, while
    the pi
    parent host has a user interface.

    The */subzero command* lists the tasks of the session core, prints the
    attach command of one task, and cancels every task of the session core or
    one
    by its task id.

    The *pi-subagents* extension is the existing pi extension that also gives
    the pi
    parent host a tool named subagent.

    The *extension factory* is the function that pi calls each time it loads or
    reloads PiExtension, and it gives pi the tools and commands of the
    extension.

    A *clash warning* says that another extension provides the subagent tool or
    that
    pi-subagents is still loaded, names which extension owns the subagent tool
    and
    says to remove pi-subagents. The /subzero command repeats it.

    A *turn trigger* is the setting on a message sent into a pi session that
    makes
    pi start a model turn when it is idle.

    The *isolation error* is the error that says isolation is not supported
    yet,
    which the subagent tool returns for a request for a worktree, for worktree
    isolation or for a fork.

    The *parallel execution mode* of pi runs the tool calls of one message at
    the
    same time. The *peer dependencies* of a pi package are the packages that it
    relies on pi to provide instead of bundling them.

    A *print mode* is a pi session with no user interface that runs one prompt
    and
    exits, such as pi -p or the json mode.
  }

  logic {
    On the start of a pi session, the entry point builds the session core and
    hands
    it to PiExtension, which checks the registered tools and commands for a
    clash warning and shows it, and gives the subagent tool a description that
    lists
    each
    tier word with the model tier it maps to, or says that a tier word whose
    model tier is not configured should omit its model, and says to await
    background
    tasks
    with subzero_await before using their results. The flow ends there.

    On a subagent tool call, refuse it with the isolation error when it asks
    for a
    worktree, for worktree isolation or for a fork, and refuse a call that sets
    a
    management field, such as action or a workflow field, with a message that
    points
    to the subzero tools, which ends the flow. Map its agent name through
    AgentConfig, so that an agent alias names the general agent, and map its
    tier text to a model tier. An unmatched tier text is treated as no tier text,
    and the
    reply says the value was not used. Make a delegation with the brief text,
    the
    mapped agent name and model tier, the files, the expected output and the
    parent session id of the session core, and send it to the session core. The
    flow
    returns the task id at once, or the result text when the call sets async to
    false, and it ends there.

    When a task that the call did not wait for settles, send its
    completion notice
    into the pi session with a turn trigger as a steering message, so that it
    starts
    a turn when pi is idle and joins the turn that is running otherwise, which
    ends
    that flow. A task that ended by a session cancel after an abort, or by a
    cancel
    through the subzero tools or the /subzero command, sends no turn trigger:
    its
    stop notice is shown to the user, and the parent model gets one stop notice
    for
    each stopped task on its next turn, which ends that flow. A task that ends
    with
    the pi session sends no stop notice to the parent model, and the user sees
    only
    the count of cancelled tasks.

    When a turn of the pi session settles as aborted by the user, run a
    session cancel for the session core, which ends the flow.

    On the end of a pi session, for any reason, including a new session, a
    resumed
    session, a fork and a reload, run a session cancel, shut the session core
    down,
    which records every task that was still live as cancelled and ends the
    child runs
    that are left, and show the user how many tasks were cancelled, which ends
    the
    flow.
  }

  constraints {
    PiExtension requires its entry point to build every part of the
    session core
    inside the extension factory or on the start of a pi session, never at the
    top
    level of its module, so that a reload that runs the factory again never
    meets a
    Kernel that already holds the parent adapter pi.

    PiExtension must give the working directory of the pi session as the sole
    root for DelegationService to resolve the project root, and must not read
    SUBZERO_PROJECT_DIR, because that setting
    may
    leak in from the shell that started pi.

    A pi project with no agent file must be refused with the load error that
    says to
    run subzero init, and PiExtension must never run a subagent on a model that
    the
    agent file does not name. A malformed agent file must still return its
    load error, and a name that the agent file does not hold must still run the
    fallback agent.

    PiExtension must reach the core only through the session core and
    AgentConfig,
    and it must never be given a child driver: its entry point holds each
    child driver, and it names no child host.

    The subagent tool must run in pi's parallel execution mode, so that several
    calls
    in one message start their children at the same time, up to each
    parallel limit.

    In a print mode, every subagent tool call must wait for its result,
    whatever its
    async flag says, and the reply must say so when async was set, because a
    child
    left running in the background would be killed when pi exits.

    A completion notice and a stop notice must never be sent after the end of
    the pi
    session that started their task, so that no notice crosses into another
    session.
    Neither may carry the transcript of a child run.

    The session widget must be shown only when the pi parent host has a user
    interface. The clash warning must always be shown: as a notification when
    the pi
    parent host has a user interface, and on the error stream in a print mode.

    PiExtension must ship as a *pi package* from a git branch, built from the
    same
    source as each other parent adapter, and the pi package must list pi's own
    packages as peer dependencies and not bundle them.
  }

  cases {
    With the model tier small configured on a local model, a subagent tool call
    whose
    model is cheapest capable starts a child on that local model and returns
    its task id at once.

    In a project with no agent file, a subagent tool call returns the
    load error that
    says to run subzero init and starts no child.

    With the medium tier configured, a subagent tool call with no model runs on
    the
    medium tier, and a call that names the agent reviewer, whose own tier is
    small,
    and no model runs on small.

    A subagent tool call with the model anthropic/claude-opus, an
    unmatched tier text,
    runs as a call with no model would: the general agent runs on the
    medium tier and
    the agent reviewer runs on its own tier small, and the reply says the value
    was
    not used.

    A subagent tool call that asks for worktree isolation or a fork fails with
    the
    isolation error and starts no child.

    With three tasks running in the background and pi idle, the first task to
    settle
    sends a completion notice that starts a turn, names the two tasks still
    running
    and says to wait for them.

    With two background tasks from an earlier turn and one from the current
    turn, a
    turn aborted by the user ends all three as cancelled, sends no
    turn trigger, and
    the parent model gets three stop notices on its next turn, one for each
    task.

    With pi idle and two background tasks running, the /subzero command with
    cancel
    ends both as cancelled and reports 2, and no turn starts.

    With one background task running, a new pi session runs a session cancel
    that ends
    it as cancelled and shows that one task was cancelled.

    In a print mode, a subagent tool call that sets async waits and returns the
    result text.

    With pi-subagents installed, the start of a pi session shows the
    clash warning
    whether or not PiExtension owns the subagent tool, and the warning names
    the
    extension that owns it.

    Each task that the subagent tool starts is in the task record under the
    parent session id of the pi session, and the subzero command line lists it.
  }

  interface {
    Give the pi parent host the subagent tool, which takes a brief text and an
    optional agent name, tier text, async flag, files and expected output, and
    returns
    a task id at once or, with async set to false, the result text.

    Give the pi parent host the subzero tools to collect, list and cancel the
    tasks of
    its session core, each reply about a task with no result giving its
    status line
    and never calling a queued task started.

    Deliver the completion notice of each background task into the pi session,
    and the
    stop notice of each task that was stopped, under the rules of the logic.

    Run a session cancel when the user aborts a turn, when the /subzero command
    asks
    for one, and at the end of each pi session.

    Show the session widget while pi has a user interface, show any
    clash warning in
    every pi session, and offer the /subzero command to list, attach and cancel
    tasks.

    Be registered with Kernel as the parent adapter pi by the entry point of
    the pi package, which also creates the Kernel and registers the child driver of
    each
    child host it supports, and be installed from its pi package. The
    entry point
    builds the Kernel and the child drivers inside the extension factory,
    builds the
    session core at the start of each pi session, and hands PiExtension only
    that
    session core.
  }

  decisions {
    PiExtension replaces pi-subagents for compound-engineering and owns the
    name
    subagent, because compound-engineering asks for subagent in pi and a second
    tool
    name would be bypassed. pi keeps only the first extension that registers a
    tool
    name, so the clash warning is the only signal when the two are both loaded.

    Background is the default, as in pi-subagents, and each finished task wakes
    the
    parent model with a completion notice that lists the tasks still running,
    so the
    model reacts to each result but waits for the rest. A stopped task does not
    wake
    the model, because a person who stops everything must not see the model
    start
    again.

    An unconfigured model tier returns the tier error, and an
    unmatched tier text is ignored and reported in the reply, so that a typo or
    an unknown model never moves work to a more
    expensive
    model. The medium tier runs work that names no tier, so
    compound-engineering works
    in every project once subzero init has written the agent file. The
    session core
    lives for one pi session and is cancelled at its end, because the pi
    process
    outlives a session and a child left running would keep a running
    task record with
    a live owner.

    pi gives an extension no event for Escape while it is idle, so Escape stops
    every
    child only during a turn, and the /subzero command stops them while pi is
    idle.

    A project with no agent file is refused until subzero init writes one, so
    that the
    starter tools of the general agent, which may write files and run shell
    commands,
    are always the ones that the agent file names. Installing the pi package is
    the
    opt-in that accepts this. Capping the tools of a child to the active tools
    of the
    pi session is left for a later change.
  }
}
